LGPL dependency (binary redistribution only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A built `pxsmith` binary links `ansi_colours` (LGPL-3.0-or-later) through
`viuer` -> `pxsmith-view`. Rust links statically, so redistributing such a
binary carries the LGPL-3.0 obligation to let recipients relink it against a
modified `ansi_colours` (LGPL section 4). No prebuilt binaries are distributed
by this project; `cargo install` builds on the user's own machine.

Publishing source to a registry does not convey a Combined Work, so the source
crates themselves do not carry that obligation.

The dependency enters through exactly one path, and it can be switched off:

  ansi_colours (LGPL-3.0-or-later)
    <- viuer (MIT)
       <- pxsmith-view, feature "terminal" (on by default)
          <- pxsmith

`pxsmith-view` reaches `viuer` only from `term::detect` and `term::show`.
Building it with `--no-default-features` removes `viuer` and `ansi_colours`
from the dependency tree entirely, leaving `render`, `diff`, `onion` and
`TerminalKind` available. Every other published crate has no LGPL in its tree
under any feature combination:

  pxsmith-core / pxsmith-io / pxsmith-lint / pxsmith-recipe / pxsmith-macro
  / pxsmith-gen                                     -- no LGPL in the tree
  pxsmith-view (default features) / pxsmith         -- LGPL via viuer
  pxsmith-view --no-default-features                -- no LGPL in the tree

`icy_sixel` (MIT OR Apache-2.0) is reachable only through the optional
`icy_sixel` / `sixel` features of `pxsmith-view`, which are off by default.
